---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'June 16, 2025';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy — AstraLumen Science Review Standards"
  description="Learn how AstraLumen ensures scientific accuracy through expert review, fact-checking, sourcing standards, and editorial oversight."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial Policy' }]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Trust & Accuracy</span>
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        How we research, write, review, and maintain scientifically accurate educational content.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        At {SITE.name}, scientific accuracy is our highest priority. Every article published on
        our platform goes through a rigorous editorial process designed to ensure that learners,
        educators, and curious readers receive trustworthy, up-to-date science education.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Editorial Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accuracy first</strong> — Facts must be verifiable against peer-reviewed literature, government agencies, or established scientific institutions.</li>
        <li><strong>Clarity without oversimplification</strong> — We make complex science accessible without sacrificing precision.</li>
        <li><strong>Transparency</strong> — We cite sources, disclose author credentials, and identify when scientific consensus is evolving.</li>
        <li><strong>Independence</strong> — Editorial decisions are not influenced by advertisers or sponsors.</li>
        <li><strong>Inclusivity</strong> — Science education should be welcoming to learners of all backgrounds and ages.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content Creation Process</h2>
      <h3>1. Topic Selection</h3>
      <p>
        Topics are chosen based on educational value, reader interest, curriculum relevance, and
        alignment with current scientific understanding. We prioritize evergreen content that
        remains accurate and useful over time.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Research & Writing</h3>
      <p>
        Articles are researched using primary sources including peer-reviewed journals (via PubMed,
        arXiv, NASA, NOAA, USGS, and institutional repositories), government science agencies,
        and textbooks from accredited institutions. Writers hold advanced degrees in relevant
        scientific fields or have equivalent professional experience.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Expert Review</h3>
      <p>
        Every article is reviewed by at least one subject-matter expert from our
        <a href="/authors">editorial team</a> before publication. Reviewers verify:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Factual accuracy of scientific claims</li>
        <li>Appropriate use of terminology and units</li>
        <li>Balanced presentation of established science vs. emerging research</li>
        <li>Age-appropriate language and explanations</li>
        <li>Completeness of references and citations</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4. Fact-Checking</h3>
      <p>
        A dedicated fact-checking step verifies specific claims, statistics, dates, and names
        against primary sources. Numerical data (distances, temperatures, masses, etc.) is
        cross-referenced with authoritative databases such as NASA Planetary Fact Sheets and
        NIST reference data.
      </p>

      <h3>5. Publication & Updates</h3>
      <p>
        Published articles display the author's name, reviewer credentials, publication date, and
        last updated date. We review and update content when significant new research emerges or
        when readers report errors through our <a href="/corrections-policy">corrections policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Sourcing Standards</h2>
      <p>We prioritize sources in the following order:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Peer-reviewed scientific journals and conference proceedings</li>
        <li>Government science agencies (NASA, NOAA, NIH, EPA, USGS, ESA, etc.)</li>
        <li>University and research institution publications</li>
        <li>Established science textbooks and encyclopedias</li>
        <li>Reputable science journalism (for context, not as primary evidence)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        We avoid citing unverified blogs, social media posts, or sources with known conflicts of
        interest as primary references.
      </p>

      <h2>Handling Evolving Science</h2>
      <p>
        Science advances continuously. When a topic is actively debated or newly discovered, we
        clearly indicate the current state of research and distinguish between established
        consensus and emerging findings. Articles on rapidly evolving topics (such as climate
        science or exoplanet research) are reviewed more frequently.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        When errors are identified, we correct them promptly and transparently. Minor corrections
        are noted with an updated date. Significant corrections receive an editor's note at the
        top of the article. See our full <a href="/corrections-policy">Corrections Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising & Editorial Independence</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} may display advertisements to support free access to our content. Advertisers
        have no influence over editorial content, topic selection, or review outcomes. Sponsored
        content, if ever published, will be clearly labeled.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact the Editorial Team</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about our editorial standards? Reach out at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or visit our
        <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: var(--space-lg) auto var(--space-sm);
  }

  .hero-meta {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .section {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4xl);
  }
</style>
